{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"a99d7f42580294766aaa0828b7c2262e7f843fff303b87b8506ab78517959388","slug":"chapters.preface.what-is-programming","location":"/chapters/preface/what_is_programming.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Was ist Programmieren?","content_includes_title":false,"numbering":{"title":{"enabled":true,"offset":1},"equation":{"enabled":true,"continue":true}},"keywords":["python","chemistry","jupyter-book"],"enumerator":"0.2","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"what_is_programming.md","url":"/python_for_chemists//build/what_is_programming-82f61aef24e4a2aefd6079663e5c0108.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","kind":"caution","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under Construction","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"lHwF9GrX5C"}],"key":"H9wUUTo0ym"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Diese Seite befindet sich noch im Aufbau. Bitte haben Sie etwas Geduld, bis sie vollständig ist.","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"EdhEujxVQW"}],"key":"e0eBGfq0y3"}],"key":"DQnkzbTFbr"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Programmieren bedeutet, einem Computer Anweisungen so aufzuschreiben, dass er sie Schritt für Schritt ausführen kann. Diese Anweisungen werden in einer Textdatei gespeichert und bilden zusammen ein Programm.","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"B63TMnQ0ZH"}],"key":"MgEmKNcyaK"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ein Computer verarbeitet Informationen nach festen Regeln. Er “versteht” nicht, was wir meinen, sondern führt nur genau die Befehle aus, die ihm gegeben werden.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"tmrCEK8weS"}],"key":"B5Up5JdRP9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Python ist eine Programmiersprache, also eine bestimmte Art, solche Anweisungen zu formulieren. Sie ist gut lesbar und deshalb besonders geeignet, um die Grundlagen des Programmierens zu lernen.","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"Cifhax3juY"}],"key":"WqQsTMpNDD"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wenn Sie ein Python-Programm starten, liest der Computer den Code und arbeitet die Befehle der Reihe nach ab. So lassen sich Berechnungen automatisieren, Daten auswerten und wiederholbare Abläufe zuverlässig ausführen.","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"bzNuIKc07A"}],"key":"Muer6fm6pP"}],"key":"wxRs6Ll6ux"}],"key":"ifBb1plyD7"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Motivation","url":"/chapters/preface/motivation","group":"Programmierkurs für Chemiker"},"next":{"title":"Software-Installation und Einrichtung","url":"/chapters/preface/software-setup","group":"Programmierkurs für Chemiker"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}